in being technically speaking villains in a DC campaign, so it wouldn't be fair for them to fight against something that doesn't have stats...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T16:27:03-07:00","id":1519675,"title":"","content":"Narrow it down to a few desired powers per person, that'll make suggestions easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T18:26:06-07:00","id":1519689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rosencroft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1519669-chronicles-of-dark-justice-league?p=1519674#post1519674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My players are interested in being technically speaking villains in a DC campaign, so it wouldn't be fair for them to fight against something that doesn't have stats...</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, i'm of the opinion the Kamen Rider series (and possibly also a number of other tokusatsu) is much more Deviant ressonant than the League.<br /> <br /> Heroes of the Marvel universe, either groups like the Defenders or Fantastic Four or a number of individual vigilantes like Spider-Man, Luke Cage, Daredevil and countless others should make great fits too.<br /> <br /> Not saying DC Heroes could not work, but Marvel does play more with human fragility, feet of clay, power has a price, victims of circunstances &amp; life getting in the way angles in general, what had an influence through crosspolination in 60s-70s TV and manga media, believe it or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T19:45:25-07:00","id":1519701,"title":"","content":"Martian Manhunter could be a powerful psychic who is now insane (he really believes he's from Mars). The shape-shifting powers are illusions he projects into people's minds. His strength and resilience are based on Telekinesis.<br /> <br /> Aquaman could have fish and marine mammal DNA. Thus allowing his aquatic powers.<br /> <br /> Flash could be possessed by an entity with time distortion powers. It just looks like superspeed to those in normal time.<br /> <br /> Wonder Woman, Green Lantern, and Superman, also work best as possessed by powerful spirt beings.<br /> <br /> Batman, I'd handle differently, he's another insane psychic. His insanity is Multiple personality disorder. His alternate personalities are the Joker, Poison Ivy, Mr. Freeze, the Penguin, Two-Face, the Scarecrow, Harley Quin, Clayface, the Mad Hatter, and Catwoman. Bruce is lost. Batman controls Arkham Asylum (his subconscious) and Alfred talks to the group. Alfred decides which of the villians comes out to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-03-2023, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}